// A history-dependent rule — refuse a write once six writes have completed in the
// last 60 seconds.
//
// The cap is a `forbid`, because a permit only adds permission: a
// `permit … when temporal { total < 6 }` beside a broader `fs:write` permit caps
// nothing, and the box refuses that shape at load. A `forbid` beats every permit, so
// this rule holds beside `agent-anthropic.dw` or any other write permit.
//
// The count walks `fs:write::response` events. A `::response` exists only for an effect
// that happened, because only a recorded outcome emits one. Keying on `::request`
// instead would count a denied attempt, so a budget written against `::request` is
// defeated by asking and being refused.
//
// `formerly within 60s` bounds the window. A window is mandatory, and it is also what
// keeps the engine's retained history bounded.
//
// A temporal predicate names one granular action, offers no group, no `||`, and no
// wildcard. Every field it reads is derived from the action's `input` record.

@id("write_budget")
@description("This workload has reached its write budget of six writes in 60 seconds. Wait a minute before the next write, or batch the remaining writes into one call.")
forbid (principal, action == Box::Action::"fs:write", resource)
when temporal {
    exists (total: Long). (
        (count for (t: Timepoint). where (
            formerly within 60s (
                Box::Action::"fs:write"::response{ input.path: _, input.operation: Box::FsWriteOperation::"write_content" } && tp(t)
            )
        )) == total
        && total >= 6
    )
};
